<p>(a) $ in millions Development and Acquisition Activity</p>
<p>During the quarter the company acquired the newly developed 128 room Courtyard by Marriott in Wilmington, N.C.  For the year, the hotel portfolio grew by 48% to 31 hotels, while the inventory of rooms grew by 49% to 4,026.  Winston currently has under development four high-end, extended-stay Homewood Suites Hotels with 456 suites, two of which are scheduled to be completed during the latter part of 1997 and the other two for early in 1998.  In addition the company has a contract to purchase a 123 suite Homewood Suites Hotel from Promus Company Inc. upon its completion, which is scheduled for the third quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>Divided Performance</p>
<p>Also, during the fourth quarter Winston Hotels announced its regular quarterly cash dividend of $0.255, which was paid on Jan. 14, 1997 to stockholders of record as of Dec. 30, 1996.  The regular quarterly dividend is equivalent to $1.02 on an annualized basis.</p>
